            "body": "> haven't seen any upvotes on #36181 so demand seems weak.\r\n\r\nthe original https://github.com/Davidyz/inlayhint-filler.nvim has 53, so it seems like there is some damned (even if it is not as big as the new great MC feature :)\r\nI mainly use this to insert inferred type hints in python so I can be more explicit / edit them a bit. Before starting to use a version of this feature I had my own hacky solution that parsed the hints from the virtual text of the inlay hint, so this is already a huge improvement for me.\r\n\r\n\r\n> this is a lot of code so ideally should find ways to shrink it. i already found 2 cases that look like potential code duplication.\r\n\r\nI also noticed the same duplication, but I afraid it was out of scope for the PR.\r\nNow that I know it is fine (and even desired) to refactor code outside of the inlay-hint module, I have extracted the functions mentioned.\r\nIn addition, I extracted and combined:\r\n- the markdown rendering used here and in `vim.lsp.buf.hover`. \r\n- the ordered async task collection used `codelens`.\r\n\r\nI have also made various fixes to possible race conditions / stale data usage.\r\nUnfortunately this further increased the size of the PR.\r\nI will try to simplify the code, but I'm a bit out of ideas, so suggestion would be greatly appreciated :) ",
            "created_at": "2026-10-11T08:37:57Z",
